      "title": "Cat-qubit machine could crack RSA-2048 with about 22,600 qubits",
      "summary": "Researchers compiled Shor's algorithm for superconducting cat qubits and estimated that about 22,593 qubits could break RSA-2048 encryption in roughly 3.14 days. The company behind it says this needs far fewer physical qubits than Google's 2025 estimate, which tightens the timeline for quantum-safe security planning. It is still a paper estimate, because no machine today has anywhere near that many error-corrected qubits.",
